Layoffs Data Exploratory Data Analysis Using SQL
Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing a global layoffs dataset using SQL to uncover trends, patterns, and insights related to workforce reductions across companies and industries. The analysis helps understand how layoffs changed over time and which sectors, countries, and companies were most affected.

The project demonstrates practical SQL skills used in real-world data analytics and business intelligence workflows.

Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

Analyze overall layoff trends
Identify companies with the highest layoffs
Discover industries most affected by layoffs
Compare layoffs across countries
Track layoffs over time using yearly and monthly analysis
Identify companies with complete workforce reductions
Rank companies based on yearly layoffs
Perform cumulative trend analysis
Dataset Description

The dataset contains information about layoffs from companies around the world. It includes details such as:

Company name
Industry
Country
Date of layoffs
Total employees laid off
Percentage of employees laid off
Funding raised
Company stage

The dataset was cleaned and prepared before performing exploratory analysis.

Analysis Performed

The project includes multiple SQL-based analyses to explore the dataset from different perspectives.

Data Inspection

Initial exploration was performed to understand the structure and contents of the dataset.

Maximum Layoff Analysis

The analysis identified:

The highest number of employees laid off in a single event
The highest layoff percentage recorded
Complete Company Shutdowns

Companies with 100% layoffs were analyzed to identify businesses that completely shut down operations.

Company-Wise Layoff Analysis

Total layoffs were calculated for each company to identify organizations with the largest workforce reductions.

Industry Analysis

Layoffs were grouped by industry to determine which sectors were impacted the most.

Country Analysis

Layoffs were analyzed country-wise to compare the global impact.

Time-Based Analysis

Layoff trends were explored using:

Daily analysis
Monthly analysis
Yearly analysis

This helped identify periods with significant workforce reductions.

Stage-Based Analysis

Companies were analyzed based on their funding or business stage to understand how layoffs varied among startups, public companies, and late-stage organizations.

Rolling Total Analysis

Cumulative layoffs over time were calculated to observe long-term trends and growth in layoffs.

Ranking Analysis

Companies were ranked yearly based on total layoffs using SQL window functions to identify the top affected organizations each year.

SQL Concepts Used

This project demonstrates the use of several important SQL concepts, including:

Aggregate Functions
Group By Operations
Sorting and Ordering
Date Functions
Common Table Expressions (CTEs)
Window Functions
Ranking Functions
Rolling Calculations
Partitioning
Key Insights

Some important insights discovered during the analysis include:

Certain industries experienced significantly larger layoffs than others
Major technology companies contributed heavily to overall layoffs
Some companies shut down completely after receiving substantial funding.
Layoffs increased sharply during specific years and months
The impact of layoffs varied greatly across countries and company stages
